1
00:00:03,796 --> 00:00:04,755
I'm ready.

2
00:00:04,797 --> 00:00:06,674
You sure?
Uh-huh.

3
00:00:06,715 --> 00:00:09,593
Okay, let me just straighten
out your helmet there.

4
00:00:09,635 --> 00:00:10,803
Thanks, Daddy.

5
00:00:10,845 --> 00:00:13,472
No, no. One daddy,
two mommies.

6
00:00:14,723 --> 00:00:15,683
All right...

7
00:00:15,724 --> 00:00:16,684
it's all yours.

8
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,185
Okay. Okay.

9
00:00:18,226 --> 00:00:20,521
There you go! There you go!
There you go!

10
00:00:20,562 --> 00:00:21,856
Phoebe:
Ben's first

11
00:00:21,897 --> 00:00:24,316
big kid's bike--
This is so exciting.

12
00:00:24,358 --> 00:00:26,527
Oh, yeah.
I remember mine.

13
00:00:26,568 --> 00:00:28,821
It was my sixth birthday,
my dad took me to the park

14
00:00:28,863 --> 00:00:30,447
and I got on it and...

15
00:00:30,489 --> 00:00:31,949
it bent.

16
00:00:31,991 --> 00:00:33,784
Yeah.

17
00:00:33,826 --> 00:00:35,619
I never had a bike of my own.

18
00:00:35,661 --> 00:00:36,537
What?!

19
00:00:36,578 --> 00:00:37,746
Well, we didn't have

20
00:00:37,788 --> 00:00:39,414
a lot of money, you know.

21
00:00:39,456 --> 00:00:41,542
But the girl across the street
had the best bike.

22
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:45,086
It was pink, and it had
rainbow-colored tassels

23
00:00:45,128 --> 00:00:47,673
hanging off the handle grips,
and-and-and a bell

24
00:00:47,715 --> 00:00:49,800
and this big, white
wicker basket

25
00:00:49,842 --> 00:00:52,594
with those plastic daisies
stuck on... ooh!

26
00:00:52,636 --> 00:00:56,015
Oh, that sounds like
my first bike.

27
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:58,642
My dad gave me
his old one.

28
00:00:58,684 --> 00:01:00,519
Did the girl
ever let you ride it?

29
00:01:00,561 --> 00:01:02,021
No.

30
00:01:02,062 --> 00:01:04,356
But she gave me the box
that it came in.

31
00:01:04,398 --> 00:01:06,942
It had a picture of the bike
on the front.

32
00:01:08,736 --> 00:01:10,278
So I would sit on it

33
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:13,114
and my stepdad would drag me
around the backyard.

34
00:01:13,156 --> 00:01:15,075
That is so unfair.

35
00:01:15,116 --> 00:01:17,452
Not really.
I got to drag him around, too.

36
00:01:23,959 --> 00:01:29,088
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

37
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:31,508
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

38
00:01:31,550 --> 00:01:33,844
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

39
00:01:33,886 --> 00:01:38,557
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

40
00:01:38,599 --> 00:01:41,894
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

41
00:01:41,936 --> 00:01:44,187
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

42
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:47,524
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

43
00:01:47,566 --> 00:01:53,614
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

44
00:02:02,414 --> 00:02:04,374
Hey, what are you guys doing?

45
00:02:04,416 --> 00:02:07,335
Making holiday candy
for the neighbors.

46
00:02:07,377 --> 00:02:08,837
I'm sorry, who?

47
00:02:10,213 --> 00:02:12,049
I'm going to hang this basket
on the door

48
00:02:12,091 --> 00:02:15,010
and then when the neighbors
walk by, they can all
take a piece.

49
00:02:16,887 --> 00:02:18,931
But we don't know the neighbors.

50
00:02:18,973 --> 00:02:20,474
I do.

51
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:23,518
There's, uh... let's see,
Guy With a Mustache

52
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:24,812
Smokes-A-Lot Lady...

53
00:02:24,853 --> 00:02:26,563
some kids I've seen...

54
00:02:26,605 --> 00:02:30,442
and a red-haired guy who does
not like to be called "Rusty."

55
00:02:30,484 --> 00:02:32,945
See? This is exactly why
I'm making this candy.

56
00:02:32,987 --> 00:02:35,906
We can learn their names
and get to know our neighbors.

57
00:02:35,948 --> 00:02:38,492
Wouldn't it be easier
if we just moved?

58
00:02:40,577 --> 00:02:43,330
Good morning.

59
00:02:43,371 --> 00:02:45,707
Ah, somebody's
in a good mood.

60
00:02:45,749 --> 00:02:46,875
Well, why shouldn't I be?

61
00:02:46,917 --> 00:02:48,502
I have great friends

62
00:02:48,543 --> 00:02:50,087
I have a wonderful job--

63
00:02:50,129 --> 00:02:52,171
Where you can make out
with your assistant.

64
00:02:52,213 --> 00:02:53,340
Oh...

65
00:02:53,381 --> 00:02:54,842
Come on,
it's not a big deal.

66
00:02:54,883 --> 00:02:57,011
We stayed up all night
coming up with a plan

67
00:02:57,052 --> 00:02:58,971
so that us dating
will not be a problem.

68
00:02:59,013 --> 00:03:01,180
Oh, yeah?
What's the plan?

69
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:03,266
( exhales )

70
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:05,560
We...

71
00:03:05,602 --> 00:03:08,480
we are not...

72
00:03:08,522 --> 00:03:10,482
going to let it...

73
00:03:10,524 --> 00:03:12,442
be a problem.

74
00:03:12,484 --> 00:03:15,821
Wow, it took you
all night to come
up with that plan?

75
00:03:15,863 --> 00:03:17,156
Oh, well

76
00:03:17,196 --> 00:03:19,198
you know,
we did other stuff, too.

77
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,408
( snickering )

78
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:21,576
Did you two...

79
00:03:21,618 --> 00:03:22,953
Oh, Monica, come on.

80
00:03:22,995 --> 00:03:24,371
I don't sleep with guys
on the first date.

81
00:03:24,412 --> 00:03:26,123
Matt Wire, Mark Lynn,
Ben Wyatt...

82
00:03:26,165 --> 00:03:27,206
Anymore!

83
00:03:27,248 --> 00:03:29,292
Okay.

84
00:03:33,964 --> 00:03:35,423
Hi. Tag, um...

85
00:03:35,465 --> 00:03:37,592
I have a conference call today.
Is that correct?

86
00:03:37,634 --> 00:03:38,760
Yes, at 4:00.

87
00:03:38,802 --> 00:03:39,970
Okay, thank you.
That'll be all.

88
00:03:41,471 --> 00:03:42,556
Wait. Wait.

89
00:03:42,597 --> 00:03:44,265
( restrained giggle )

90
00:03:46,894 --> 00:03:47,936
Did you see that?

91
00:03:47,978 --> 00:03:49,270
That mail guy
had no idea

92
00:03:49,312 --> 00:03:51,481
there was something
going on between us.

93
00:03:58,488 --> 00:04:00,407
I'm going to get back
to my desk.

94
00:04:00,448 --> 00:04:02,659
Okay, hard worker.

95
00:04:04,578 --> 00:04:06,621
I'll remember to put that
in your evaluation.

96
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:07,998
My what?

97
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:10,042
Well, you've been here
for two months now

98
00:04:10,084 --> 00:04:11,376
and your boss is required

99
00:04:11,418 --> 00:04:13,128
to hand in
a performance evaluation.

100
00:04:13,170 --> 00:04:14,922
But, you know...

101
00:04:14,963 --> 00:04:17,883
there is one thing
that I have yet to evaluate.

102
00:04:23,013 --> 00:04:24,556
( laughs )

103
00:04:24,598 --> 00:04:25,933
Are you serious?

104
00:04:25,974 --> 00:04:27,976
No. I've just always
wanted to do that.

105
00:04:29,269 --> 00:04:30,938
Can you help me clean this up?

106
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:38,237
The basket is
totally empty!

107
00:04:38,277 --> 00:04:40,280
My God, the neighbors
ate all the candy!

108
00:04:40,321 --> 00:04:42,032
Well, either that, or, uh...

109
00:04:43,867 --> 00:04:45,744
Joey!

110
00:04:47,037 --> 00:04:48,997
Did you eat
Yeah.

111
00:04:49,039 --> 00:04:50,165
all the neighbor candy?

112
00:04:50,207 --> 00:04:52,000
Uh, well, yeah,
that was the plan

113
00:04:52,042 --> 00:04:53,627
but by the time
I got to it

114
00:04:53,668 --> 00:04:55,754
there was only
a couple pieces left.

115
00:04:55,796 --> 00:04:58,173
Yeah, they've been
coming by all day.
They love it.

116
00:04:58,215 --> 00:05:00,968
They love my candy?

117
00:05:01,009 --> 00:05:03,095
Oh, man! I got
to go make more!

118
00:05:03,137 --> 00:05:04,429
Hey, Mon...

119
00:05:04,471 --> 00:05:06,347
you might want to make
some more lasagna, too

120
00:05:06,389 --> 00:05:07,348
because something
might have happened

121
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:10,560
to a huge chunk
of it.

122
00:05:10,602 --> 00:05:12,479
Ross, the neighbors
ate all my candy.

123
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:14,231
Mine stole my newspaper.

124
00:05:14,273 --> 00:05:16,024
It's like a crime wave.

125
00:05:19,945 --> 00:05:22,447
Pheebs, you, uh...
you got a second?

126
00:05:22,489 --> 00:05:24,407
Sure.
Yeah...

127
00:05:24,449 --> 00:05:27,577
ever since you, uh... told me
that story about that bike

128
00:05:27,619 --> 00:05:29,496
I couldn't stop
thinking about it.

129
00:05:29,537 --> 00:05:32,124
I mean, everyone
should have a first
bike, you know?

130
00:05:32,166 --> 00:05:34,168
So...

131
00:05:35,752 --> 00:05:37,171
( gasping )

132
00:05:37,212 --> 00:05:39,173
Oh, my God, Ross!

133
00:05:39,214 --> 00:05:40,548
You like it?

134
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:41,842
I love it!

135
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:42,884
Yeah?

136
00:05:42,926 --> 00:05:43,969
Oh!

137
00:05:44,011 --> 00:05:46,221
Oh... And I love you.

138
00:05:46,263 --> 00:05:47,973
Not that way.

139
00:05:49,266 --> 00:05:50,684
But the bike got you
a lot closer.

140
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:51,643
Ah!

141
00:05:51,685 --> 00:05:54,146
Well, take it
downstairs.

142
00:05:54,188 --> 00:05:56,190
You know, give it
a... test drive.

143
00:05:56,231 --> 00:05:57,191
Okay.

144
00:05:57,232 --> 00:05:58,566
Oh, my God.

145
00:05:58,608 --> 00:06:00,694
My first bike!

146
00:06:00,735 --> 00:06:04,239
Thank you for the best
present I've ever gotten.

147
00:06:04,281 --> 00:06:06,574
You're welcome.

148
00:06:06,616 --> 00:06:08,576
( laughing )

149
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:10,787
Oh, and Chandler's
about to cry.

150
00:06:12,622 --> 00:06:14,624
( trembling ):
Am not.

151
00:06:17,294 --> 00:06:18,753
( knocking at door )

152
00:06:18,795 --> 00:06:20,047
Monica:
Who is that?

153
00:06:20,088 --> 00:06:21,882
Don't worry,
I'm brave.

154
00:06:21,923 --> 00:06:23,091
I am brave.

155
00:06:23,133 --> 00:06:24,343
I... I am brave.

156
00:06:24,383 --> 00:06:27,095
( rhythmic knocking on door )

157
00:06:27,137 --> 00:06:29,139
No, no, no, no, no.

158
00:06:29,181 --> 00:06:32,642
( weakly ):
Can you tell me
who is there, please?

159
00:06:32,684 --> 00:06:34,602
My name's Gary.
I live upstairs.

160
00:06:34,644 --> 00:06:36,980
Well...

161
00:06:37,022 --> 00:06:38,397
Hi.

162
00:06:38,439 --> 00:06:40,692
Hi. Do you know
what time it is?

163
00:06:40,734 --> 00:06:41,943
It's candy time.

164
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:46,573
My roommate says that they taste
like little drops of heaven.

165
00:06:46,614 --> 00:06:48,658
Oh, please.

166
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:49,784
Did you hear that?

167
00:06:49,826 --> 00:06:51,119
"Little drops of heaven."

168
00:06:51,161 --> 00:06:53,288
( both laughing )

169
00:06:53,330 --> 00:06:54,789
4:00 A.M.

170
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:55,790
So...

171
00:06:55,832 --> 00:06:57,416
can I get some candy?

172
00:06:57,458 --> 00:06:59,253
I am sorry,
but some of us

173
00:06:59,294 --> 00:07:01,796
have to get up early
and go to work.

174
00:07:01,838 --> 00:07:05,842
He does not know that
I am not "some of us."

175
00:07:07,510 --> 00:07:09,096
Um, listen, I'm sorry

176
00:07:09,137 --> 00:07:10,722
but I'll put some out
first thing in the morning.

177
00:07:10,764 --> 00:07:13,308
Well, okay, I'll swing by later.

178
00:07:13,350 --> 00:07:14,559
You live in this building?

179
00:07:14,601 --> 00:07:15,352
Mm-hmm.

180
00:07:15,394 --> 00:07:16,686
Mmm!

181
00:07:16,728 --> 00:07:18,479
Seems like I would have
remembered you.

182
00:07:20,148 --> 00:07:23,151
Mmm! Night, Gare.

183
00:07:35,496 --> 00:07:38,208
So did you read
your evaluation yet?

184
00:07:38,250 --> 00:07:40,710
No. It was marked
"confidential."

185
00:07:40,752 --> 00:07:43,046
I just sent it down
to Human Resources.

186
00:07:46,383 --> 00:07:48,135
Okay, please.
You're kidding, right?

187
00:07:48,176 --> 00:07:50,387
I wrote that one
as a joke for you.

188
00:07:50,429 --> 00:07:52,431
A joke they would appreciate?

189
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:55,474
I'm thinking "no."

190
00:07:55,516 --> 00:07:56,643
Well, what did you say?

191
00:07:56,684 --> 00:07:58,061
Um...

192
00:07:58,103 --> 00:08:01,440
I said that I thought
you were a good kisser

193
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:04,818
and that I liked
your teeny-tiny tushy.

194
00:08:04,859 --> 00:08:07,570
No, not my tushy.

195
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:09,114
Well, it gets worse.

196
00:08:09,156 --> 00:08:10,907
When asked
if you take initiative

197
00:08:10,949 --> 00:08:13,327
I wrote, "Yes, he was able
to unhook my bra

198
00:08:13,368 --> 00:08:14,953
with minimal supervision..."

199
00:08:16,704 --> 00:08:18,290
And under "Problems
with performance"

200
00:08:18,332 --> 00:08:21,251
I wrote "Dear God, I hope not."

201
00:08:21,293 --> 00:08:25,713
And then, uh... and then I drew
a little smiley face

202
00:08:25,755 --> 00:08:28,967
and then a small
pornographic sketch.

203
00:08:38,143 --> 00:08:40,561
Ross, that is so sweet of you
to get Phoebe that bike.

204
00:08:40,603 --> 00:08:41,938
When I heard
the story

205
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:43,690
I almost cried.

206
00:08:43,731 --> 00:08:45,317
Almost cried, huh?

207
00:08:45,359 --> 00:08:47,986
Hear that, Chandler?
Almost cried.

208
00:08:48,028 --> 00:08:52,491
Hey, you cry every time
somebody talks about Titanic.

209
00:08:52,531 --> 00:08:56,244
( trembling ):
Those two had only each other.

210
00:08:56,286 --> 00:08:57,662
Phoebe really likes
the bike, huh?

211
00:08:57,704 --> 00:08:59,206
Oh, yeah.

212
00:08:59,247 --> 00:09:00,665
I saw her walking it
down the street the other day.

213
00:09:00,707 --> 00:09:02,625
She had these flowers
in the basket.

214
00:09:02,667 --> 00:09:04,169
It was so cute.

215
00:09:04,211 --> 00:09:06,129
Yeah, I saw her this
morning walking it
by the park.

216
00:09:06,171 --> 00:09:07,464
( quiet laugh )

217
00:09:07,506 --> 00:09:09,924
Wait a minute.
She was walking the bike?

218
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:11,801
Both times?

219
00:09:11,843 --> 00:09:13,803
Hey, Pheebs.

220
00:09:13,845 --> 00:09:14,971
Oh, hi!

221
00:09:15,013 --> 00:09:16,890
Hi. So, you enjoying
the bike?

222
00:09:16,931 --> 00:09:18,016
Oh, uh-huh.

223
00:09:18,058 --> 00:09:19,267
So much.

224
00:09:19,309 --> 00:09:21,436
Pheebs, you, uh...

225
00:09:21,478 --> 00:09:25,065
you do know how
to ride a bike,
don't you?

226
00:09:26,358 --> 00:09:27,650
Of course.

227
00:09:27,692 --> 00:09:29,819
( uncomfortable laughter )

228
00:09:29,861 --> 00:09:31,612
Can we see
you ride it?

229
00:09:31,654 --> 00:09:33,448
Okay.

230
00:09:37,202 --> 00:09:39,204
( uncomfortable laughter )

231
00:09:47,212 --> 00:09:48,713
See?

232
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:58,848
See, this is why
I told you

233
00:09:58,890 --> 00:10:00,808
never get involved
with your assistants.

234
00:10:00,850 --> 00:10:02,352
And there is
no such thing

235
00:10:02,394 --> 00:10:04,521
as keeping secrets
when it comes to
having affairs.

236
00:10:04,563 --> 00:10:06,773
Did you hear that, Chandler?

237
00:10:07,607 --> 00:10:09,192
No such thing.

238
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:13,572
What happened?
I'm just eating candy.

239
00:10:15,156 --> 00:10:17,033
Maybe it's not as bad
as I think, you know?

240
00:10:17,075 --> 00:10:19,119
Maybe they didn't take it
the way I meant it.

241
00:10:19,160 --> 00:10:20,828
Absolutely, you know?

242
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:24,791
Because "tushy" can mean
both "ass" and "good worker."

243
00:10:26,834 --> 00:10:28,753
Oh, I just got
to get the thing back.

244
00:10:28,795 --> 00:10:29,796
Hey, Rach?
Yeah?

245
00:10:29,837 --> 00:10:31,465
That sketch you
mentioned

246
00:10:31,506 --> 00:10:33,716
might it've
looked a little
something like this?

247
00:10:33,758 --> 00:10:35,927
Oh, my God-- Joey!

248
00:10:37,554 --> 00:10:39,222
What is the matter
with you?

249
00:10:39,264 --> 00:10:41,475
( sighs )

250
00:10:41,516 --> 00:10:43,226
Well, I tell you

251
00:10:43,268 --> 00:10:45,937
this little talent came in handy
before I could afford porn.

252
00:10:45,979 --> 00:10:47,439
( knocking )

253
00:10:50,817 --> 00:10:52,193
Hi, I'm sorry.

254
00:10:52,235 --> 00:10:55,614
I know it's after hours,
but I really need candy.

255
00:10:55,655 --> 00:10:58,908
I'm sorry, I can't help you.
See, rules are rules.

256
00:10:58,950 --> 00:11:01,744
Please, I have people coming
from out of town today

257
00:11:01,786 --> 00:11:03,871
and I told them
all about your candy.

258
00:11:03,913 --> 00:11:06,707
You're kidding?
Out-of-towners, huh?

259
00:11:06,749 --> 00:11:08,418
What'd you tell them?

260
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:12,046
I told them your candy
was absolutely indescribable.

261
00:11:12,088 --> 00:11:15,258
Well, some people have
been saying it's, you know

262
00:11:15,300 --> 00:11:17,636
little drops of heaven,
but whatever.

263
00:11:17,676 --> 00:11:18,928
Please, can't you help me out?

264
00:11:18,970 --> 00:11:21,055
Hey, Chandler, do
we know that lady?

265
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:22,307
Maybe.

266
00:11:22,349 --> 00:11:24,934
Isn't she the woman
who lives below you

267
00:11:24,976 --> 00:11:26,769
and has sex really loud?

268
00:11:26,811 --> 00:11:28,522
All right, I'll do
it just this once

269
00:11:28,563 --> 00:11:30,273
but you can't tell anybody.

270
00:11:30,315 --> 00:11:31,983
Yes, yes, please,
just give it to me.

271
00:11:32,025 --> 00:11:34,944
Both:
Yeah, that's her.

272
00:11:34,986 --> 00:11:37,155
It's unbelievable.

273
00:11:37,197 --> 00:11:39,782
I can't believe
that sign didn't work.

274
00:11:39,824 --> 00:11:40,950
You know what would work?

275
00:11:40,992 --> 00:11:41,951
Hmm?

276
00:11:41,993 --> 00:11:42,994
Stop making candy.

277
00:11:43,036 --> 00:11:45,288
But they like it.

278
00:11:45,330 --> 00:11:47,499
You mean they like you.

279
00:11:47,541 --> 00:11:49,876
Maybe.

280
00:11:49,917 --> 00:11:53,463
Is that why you became a chef
so that people would like you?

281
00:11:53,505 --> 00:11:56,049
You really want to talk
about getting people

282
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:57,800
to like you, huh, funny man?

283
00:12:07,394 --> 00:12:09,979
Okay, now, just remember
everything I taught you

284
00:12:10,021 --> 00:12:11,398
and you'll be
fine, okay?

285
00:12:11,439 --> 00:12:14,817
Here we go.
Ready? Set...

286
00:12:14,859 --> 00:12:17,111
Wait, this seat is
really uncomfortable.

287
00:12:17,153 --> 00:12:20,615
Maybe, before we start,
we should just get another one?

288
00:12:20,657 --> 00:12:22,033
Perhaps like
an airplane seat

289
00:12:22,075 --> 00:12:24,952
or a beanbag chair!

290
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:27,581
Phoebe, you can't
get out of this, okay?

291
00:12:27,622 --> 00:12:29,999
You have to learn
how to ride a bike.

292
00:12:30,041 --> 00:12:33,587
Why? Why do I have to learn?

293
00:12:33,628 --> 00:12:36,339
Well, in case
of an emergency.

294
00:12:36,381 --> 00:12:38,508
What kind of emergency?

295
00:12:38,550 --> 00:12:43,346
Well, what if a man comes along
and puts a gun to your head

296
00:12:43,388 --> 00:12:46,849
and says "You ride this bike
or I'll sh--

297
00:12:46,891 --> 00:12:49,018
I'll shoot you."

298
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:51,312
Okay. I would ring the bell
to distract him

299
00:12:51,354 --> 00:12:53,814
and then I would knock the gun
out of his hand

300
00:12:53,856 --> 00:12:55,442
with a Chinese throwing star.

301
00:12:56,526 --> 00:12:58,194
Okay, Phoebe, just, just...

302
00:12:58,236 --> 00:13:02,073
get on the bike and,
hey, I'll hold you up

303
00:13:02,115 --> 00:13:03,908
and push you, okay?

304
00:13:03,950 --> 00:13:06,785
You won't let go?

305
00:13:06,827 --> 00:13:07,579
No.

306
00:13:07,621 --> 00:13:08,288
You swear?

307
00:13:08,329 --> 00:13:09,706
I swear.

308
00:13:09,748 --> 00:13:12,041
Okay.

309
00:13:12,083 --> 00:13:15,044
Come on.

310
00:13:15,086 --> 00:13:16,296
All right, here we go.

311
00:13:16,337 --> 00:13:17,297
Yeah, but hold on.

312
00:13:17,338 --> 00:13:18,298
All right?
All right.

313
00:13:18,339 --> 00:13:19,299
All right?
Mm-hmm.

314
00:13:19,340 --> 00:13:20,383
Feel good?
Well...

315
00:13:20,425 --> 00:13:21,426
All right,
try peddling.

316
00:13:21,468 --> 00:13:22,885
Okay. That's it.

317
00:13:22,927 --> 00:13:24,845
You're doing great.
Yes, yes, yes.

318
00:13:24,887 --> 00:13:26,180
Take control.

319
00:13:26,222 --> 00:13:27,348
Yes?
Whee!

320
00:13:27,390 --> 00:13:28,891
Yes! Yes!
Yay!

321
00:13:28,933 --> 00:13:31,686
Oh! Oh! Oh, no!

322
00:13:32,979 --> 00:13:34,564
You swore!

323
00:13:34,606 --> 00:13:36,232
I just thought
you were doing so well...

324
00:13:36,274 --> 00:13:40,027
I am shocked. Shocked!

325
00:13:43,906 --> 00:13:46,660
It's a legitimate
learning technique.

326
00:13:46,701 --> 00:13:48,286
Wow.

327
00:13:54,959 --> 00:13:56,043
( crowd talking )

328
00:13:56,085 --> 00:13:57,629
Hey...

329
00:13:57,671 --> 00:14:00,757
there's some people outside
asking about candy.

330
00:14:00,799 --> 00:14:02,049
Well, they're just

331
00:14:02,091 --> 00:14:03,677
going to have to wait,
aren't they?

332
00:14:03,718 --> 00:14:04,761
I've only got two hands!

333
00:14:04,803 --> 00:14:06,763
Need some help?

334
00:14:06,805 --> 00:14:08,889
No! You don't know the system!

335
00:14:08,931 --> 00:14:11,768
Don't need nobody
messing with the system!

336
00:14:11,810 --> 00:14:14,604
By the way,
the week before your wedding

337
00:14:14,646 --> 00:14:16,731
you may not see a lot of me.

338
00:14:22,362 --> 00:14:23,655
( knocks )

339
00:14:26,449 --> 00:14:29,076
Oh, hello, liar.

340
00:14:29,118 --> 00:14:35,542
Look, I'm, I'm really sorry
I let go of the bike.

341
00:14:35,583 --> 00:14:37,794
I could've been killed,
I hope you know.

342
00:14:39,337 --> 00:14:41,548
I know, I know.

343
00:14:43,550 --> 00:14:45,802
But can we please
try it again, huh?

344
00:14:45,844 --> 00:14:47,970
I mean,
you were so close, Phoebe.

345
00:14:48,012 --> 00:14:52,726
Well, I would love to,
but the bike got stolen

346
00:14:52,767 --> 00:14:54,811
and the police have no suspects.

347
00:15:00,817 --> 00:15:01,776
Phoebe?

348
00:15:01,818 --> 00:15:02,694
What?

349
00:15:02,736 --> 00:15:04,028
( bell ringing )

350
00:15:04,070 --> 00:15:07,490
What the hell?!

351
00:15:07,532 --> 00:15:09,075
All right, you know what?

352
00:15:09,116 --> 00:15:11,828
If you are not going
to learn how to ride this bike

353
00:15:11,870 --> 00:15:14,873
then I'm sorry, I'm just
going to have to take it back.

354
00:15:14,914 --> 00:15:15,874
What? Why?

355
00:15:15,915 --> 00:15:17,417
Because,
because it's...

356
00:15:17,458 --> 00:15:21,128
it'd be like you having

357
00:15:21,170 --> 00:15:22,338
this guitar

358
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:25,258
and, and never playing it.

359
00:15:25,299 --> 00:15:29,178
Okay, this guitar
wants to be played

360
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:31,305
and this bike wants

361
00:15:31,347 --> 00:15:33,516
to be ridden and, and

362
00:15:33,558 --> 00:15:38,730
if you don't ride it, you're...
you're killing its spirit.

363
00:15:40,565 --> 00:15:44,819
The bike is dying.

364
00:15:47,739 --> 00:15:49,407
All right.

365
00:15:49,449 --> 00:15:53,411
If you care enough to make up
that load of crap, okay.

366
00:15:53,453 --> 00:15:54,704
Great, great.

367
00:15:56,748 --> 00:15:59,667
You're making the bike
very happy.

368
00:15:59,709 --> 00:16:01,085
( patronizing ):
Okay, Ross.

369
00:16:03,838 --> 00:16:07,174
( whispers ):
Please don't die.

370
00:16:09,302 --> 00:16:10,845
I think we can get
the evaluation back

371
00:16:10,887 --> 00:16:12,430
before they see it

372
00:16:12,472 --> 00:16:14,098
but we'll have to get
into Mr. Zelner's office.

373
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:15,850
Now, he doesn't get in
until 10:00

374
00:16:15,892 --> 00:16:18,144
so he's no problem,
but his assistant Betty

375
00:16:18,185 --> 00:16:20,979
she comes in early to eat
her breakfast at her desk.

376
00:16:21,021 --> 00:16:22,064
That's kind of sad.

377
00:16:22,106 --> 00:16:24,901
Yeah, well, Betty's kind of sad.

378
00:16:24,943 --> 00:16:27,278
Which is why I believe
I can lure her away

379
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:28,613
with these chocolates.

380
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:32,283
Now, while I distract her,
you go in the office.

381
00:16:32,325 --> 00:16:32,951
Got it.

382
00:16:32,992 --> 00:16:33,868
Let's roll.

383
00:16:35,077 --> 00:16:37,789
Hello, Rachel.
You got a minute?

384
00:16:37,831 --> 00:16:42,376
Yeah, sure Mr. Zelner.
For you, anything... a minute.

385
00:16:42,418 --> 00:16:43,628
Okay, great.

386
00:16:43,670 --> 00:16:45,171
Abort the plan.
Abort the plan, abort...

387
00:16:45,212 --> 00:16:47,841
Actually, I'd like
to speak to both of you.

388
00:16:47,882 --> 00:16:49,216
Okay.

389
00:16:49,258 --> 00:16:53,930
Uh, well, can we get
you anything, Mr. Zelner?

390
00:16:53,972 --> 00:16:55,932
Maybe some chocolates?

391
00:16:55,974 --> 00:17:00,227
Um, no, thanks,
but I'll give these to Betty.

392
00:17:02,772 --> 00:17:05,023
So I ready your evaluation
of Tag.

393
00:17:05,065 --> 00:17:08,528
Or to use his full name,
Tag "Sweet Cheeks" Jones.

394
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:11,698
Something going on with you two?

395
00:17:11,739 --> 00:17:13,950
Oh, my God!

396
00:17:13,992 --> 00:17:18,037
Can you imagine
if there was?

397
00:17:19,664 --> 00:17:23,417
I mean,
what would happen, exactly?

398
00:17:23,459 --> 00:17:26,504
Well, I'd be forced
to file a report.

399
00:17:26,546 --> 00:17:30,299
I'd have to consult
with the legal department

400
00:17:30,341 --> 00:17:32,343
and your future at the company
would be in jeopardy.

401
00:17:34,762 --> 00:17:35,221
Well...

402
00:17:35,262 --> 00:17:36,430
Uh, Mr. Zelner

403
00:17:36,472 --> 00:17:39,099
I'm the one who filled in
that evaluation.

404
00:17:39,141 --> 00:17:40,142
Oh, no, no, no.

405
00:17:40,184 --> 00:17:42,102
Yeah, yeah, yeah,
yeah, yeah.

406
00:17:42,144 --> 00:17:43,980
I thought it
would be funny.

407
00:17:44,022 --> 00:17:47,066
You wrote that you have
"a cute tushy"?

408
00:17:48,609 --> 00:17:49,652
Yes.

409
00:17:49,694 --> 00:17:51,821
I have a weird sense of humor

410
00:17:51,863 --> 00:17:55,073
and I'm kind of
strangely proud of my butt.

411
00:17:57,243 --> 00:17:59,245
It's kind of a risky joke, Tag.

412
00:17:59,286 --> 00:18:00,496
And what is this drawing?

413
00:18:00,538 --> 00:18:02,040
I can't figure out what this is.

414
00:18:02,081 --> 00:18:04,542
You're looking at it
upside-down.

415
00:18:04,584 --> 00:18:06,836
You know what?
Doesn't matter.

416
00:18:06,878 --> 00:18:09,589
Hey, it's not like I don't
have a sense of humor, huh?

417
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:12,675
Hell, I even enjoy a naughty
limerick every now and then.

418
00:18:14,886 --> 00:18:17,555
But there's a time
and a place, huh?

419
00:18:17,597 --> 00:18:19,390
Mmm.

420
00:18:19,432 --> 00:18:22,309
Unless you had a limerick
right now.

421
00:18:23,937 --> 00:18:25,354
No?

422
00:18:25,396 --> 00:18:26,355
Okay.

423
00:18:26,397 --> 00:18:28,608
Well, you've got my fax number.

424
00:18:28,649 --> 00:18:29,943
Mmm.

425
00:18:35,239 --> 00:18:37,075
( both chuckle )

426
00:18:37,116 --> 00:18:39,285
Can't believe you did that.
That was really sweet.

427
00:18:39,326 --> 00:18:40,411
Ah, don't worry about it.

428
00:18:40,453 --> 00:18:42,789
No, you could have
lost your job.

429
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:44,164
Are you kidding me?

430
00:18:44,206 --> 00:18:45,792
With a cute butt like this,
I'd find work.

431
00:18:47,668 --> 00:18:49,211
Thank you. You're great.

432
00:18:50,922 --> 00:18:52,590
You know what?

433
00:18:52,632 --> 00:18:53,591
What?

434
00:18:53,633 --> 00:18:56,886
I feel great.

435
00:18:56,928 --> 00:18:58,220
In fact...

436
00:19:03,142 --> 00:19:04,351
What?

437
00:19:04,393 --> 00:19:06,854
I... it just... it took me
so long

438
00:19:06,896 --> 00:19:08,940
to get that desk organized.

439
00:19:08,982 --> 00:19:12,026
Oh, I'm sorry.

440
00:19:12,068 --> 00:19:14,153
There it is.

441
00:19:25,832 --> 00:19:27,291
What is going on?

442
00:19:27,333 --> 00:19:29,376
We're waiting
for the candy.

443
00:19:29,418 --> 00:19:30,795
Bring out the candy!

444
00:19:30,837 --> 00:19:33,047
Yeah, lady, give us candy!

445
00:19:33,089 --> 00:19:34,256
( all yelling )

446
00:19:34,298 --> 00:19:35,967
Candy?

447
00:19:36,009 --> 00:19:37,718
What's up, buddy?

448
00:19:37,760 --> 00:19:39,095
What are you doing?

449
00:19:39,137 --> 00:19:42,682
Getting candy.

450
00:19:42,723 --> 00:19:44,642
Get in here.

451
00:19:44,684 --> 00:19:47,854
Hey, and you cannot
smoke in here.

452
00:19:52,191 --> 00:19:53,275
Merry Christmas.

453
00:19:53,317 --> 00:19:55,194
Okay, guys,
the candy is coming.

454
00:19:55,235 --> 00:19:57,030
I just need
another 15 minutes

455
00:19:57,071 --> 00:19:58,656
for the chocolate to cool!

456
00:19:58,698 --> 00:20:00,741
( all clamoring )

457
00:20:00,783 --> 00:20:03,870
All right, everybody, just
be quiet, be quiet, be quiet!

458
00:20:03,911 --> 00:20:05,163
Pipe, pipe, pipe down!

459
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:07,040
What is the matter
with you people?

460
00:20:07,081 --> 00:20:09,834
This woman was trying
to do a nice thing for you.

461
00:20:09,876 --> 00:20:12,211
She was making candy

462
00:20:12,252 --> 00:20:14,755
so she could try
to get to know all of you

463
00:20:14,797 --> 00:20:18,051
and I'll bet that not one of you
can tell me her name.

464
00:20:18,092 --> 00:20:19,552
Am I right?

465
00:20:19,593 --> 00:20:23,097
Candy Lady?

466
00:20:23,139 --> 00:20:26,308
No, not "Candy Lady."

467
00:20:26,350 --> 00:20:29,812
If we know her,
can we have candy?

468
00:20:29,854 --> 00:20:32,481
All right, you know what?
Forget it.

469
00:20:32,523 --> 00:20:34,734
All of you forget it.
You've ruined it!

470
00:20:34,775 --> 00:20:36,819
Go home! You've ruined it!
You've ruined it!

471
00:20:36,861 --> 00:20:38,320
( clamoring )

472
00:20:38,362 --> 00:20:40,364
Go on, you guys ruined
everything! You ruined it!

473
00:20:47,080 --> 00:20:48,122
Thank you.

474
00:20:48,164 --> 00:20:50,541
You're welcome.

475
00:20:51,876 --> 00:20:53,293
Did you smoke?

476
00:20:53,335 --> 00:20:54,336
No.

477
00:20:54,378 --> 00:20:57,381
Smokes-a-lot Lady
blew smoke

478
00:20:57,423 --> 00:21:00,051
directly into my mouth.

479
00:21:00,093 --> 00:21:01,761
Are you okay?

480
00:21:01,802 --> 00:21:03,054
I'm fine now

481
00:21:03,096 --> 00:21:05,014
but it was really scary
there for a while.

482
00:21:05,056 --> 00:21:08,059
I mean, someone slipped
a threatening note
under the door.

483
00:21:08,101 --> 00:21:09,393
Oh, yeah.
Sorry about that.

484
00:21:09,435 --> 00:21:11,395
Mob mentality
or whatever.
I don't know.

485
00:21:17,944 --> 00:21:20,029
( chuckles )

486
00:21:20,071 --> 00:21:21,989
Wow!
Ooh!

487
00:21:22,031 --> 00:21:23,365
I can't believe it.

488
00:21:23,407 --> 00:21:25,034
I did it.
I rode a bike!

489
00:21:25,076 --> 00:21:27,787
I never thought
I'd be able to do that.

490
00:21:27,828 --> 00:21:29,247
Thank you, Ross.

491
00:21:29,288 --> 00:21:30,456
Oh, hey.
Don't thank me.

492
00:21:30,497 --> 00:21:32,041
Thank yourself.

493
00:21:32,083 --> 00:21:33,918
You're the one
who faced your fears

494
00:21:33,960 --> 00:21:35,461
and ultimately
overcame them.

495
00:21:35,502 --> 00:21:36,837
Don't be so corny, Ross.

496
00:21:36,879 --> 00:21:38,881
It's not
an After School Special.

497
00:21:38,923 --> 00:21:40,466
( laughs )

498
00:21:40,507 --> 00:21:44,344
( bell ringing )

